So this is a normal JavaScript behavior. If you attach an event handler on a `<a href` then:
- the event handler is first ran
- it opens a new tab if no preventDefault() was called

This means that we should do something like that:

``` js
if (event.ctrlKey === true) {
  // do nothing and open a new tab
  return;
}

// else:
// event.preventDefault
// do the refinement
```

In widgets:
- menu
- hierarchicalMenu
- refinementList
- pagination

All of them can or have links in templates
